abstract: >-
  TRACE is a Python library for pairwise philological alignment with pluggable
  language packs. It implements semi-global Needleman-Wunsch with affine gap
  penalties (Gotoh) and a multi-token abbreviation-span lookahead, returning
  alignment matches annotated with a tiered reason (exact, niqqud-stripped,
  plene/defective, abbreviation, orthographic, insertion, omission, no-match).
  The first shipped language pack covers Biblical and Rabbinic Hebrew.
